1
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:10,117
I want to see what
virtual reality is like.

2
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,720
I wonder when I first thought that.

3
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:20,420
I used to hate virtual reality
games with a vengeance,

4
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:24,115
and I blamed them for stealing
my brother away from me.

5
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:27,417
But later on I got curious.

6
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:31,420
I didn't know why my brother
loved them so much, so I figured

7
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:34,080
maybe I should see why for myself

8
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,497
I didn't know what to
expect at first but after a

9
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:46,077
while I was surprised by
how much I loved Alfheim.

10
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:52,697
Online it was amazing flying
through the sky on my very own wings

11
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:58,197
to fly as far as I wanted as high
as I wanted as fast as I wanted.

12
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:01,100
I'd give anything and everything for that

13
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:04,597
I think I get it now.

14
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:08,360
I can see why my brother
loves the virtual world

15
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:49,040
If I'm here, I won't be
able to see the future.

16
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:55,860
I won't be able to see the sun again.

17
00:01:56,360 --> 00:02:00,157
I'm going to cry.

18
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,030
Ah,

19
00:02:32,113 --> 00:02:38,420
hold

20
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:53,850
it!

21
00:02:53,933 --> 00:02:54,763
Levi!

22
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:59,980
I thought I told you not to call me
that at school, Nagata. Didn't I?

23
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:01,697
Yeah, you did.

24
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:03,700
Sorry, Suguha. Idiot!

25
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,700
I'm sorry, I meant Kirigaya!

26
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,280
What do you want?

27
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:10,227
Wait, why are you even here?

28
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:13,137
You got a release from taking
the high school entrance exams.

29
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:15,867
They're not making you
come anyway, are they?

30
00:03:16,620 --> 00:03:17,450
Sugu!

31
00:03:17,533 --> 00:03:18,363
Kirigaya!

32
00:03:18,446 --> 00:03:20,974
I need to talk to you, so
I've been waiting all morning.

33
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:23,597
Wait, you're not here
for the exams, are you?

34
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:24,510
No.

35
00:03:24,593 --> 00:03:26,577
The advisor for the kendo
club asked me to come in.

36
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:29,197
That's all well, what's up?

37
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:33,277
It's Sigurd and the others—they all
wanted to go hunting again this afternoon.

38
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:36,737
Sorry, I won't be going out
with those guys for a while.

39
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:37,797
Wait, what?

40
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:39,037
Why not?

41
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,897
I've got plans to head over to Arun.

42
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:44,537
That's why, but isn't Arun at
the base of the world tree?

43
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:46,077
Wait a second, you?

44
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,420
you Are you?

45
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:49,758
You're not going with that spriggan.

46
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:51,170
Yeah.

47
00:03:51,253 --> 00:03:52,260
Well, sort of.

48
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:54,577
I promised I'd show him how to get there.

49
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:57,601
But have you thought about
what you're doing, Lee?

50
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:02,837
Kitty Gaia, it's just so far away,

51
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:05,977
and you guys will be sleeping
together, and they'll...

52
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:08,707
Don't get any weird
ideas about it, you jerk!

53
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:13,697
Look, I've made up my
mind, and that's that.

54
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:16,133
Say hey to Sigurd and the others for me.

55
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:17,550
See you later.

56
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:32,500
All I'm doing is showing him
the way, that's all I'm doing.

57
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:54,740
Link, start!

58
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:13,690
Hey there.

59
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:15,677
Been waiting long? Not at all.

60
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:16,900
I just walked in.

61
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:19,515
Actually, I was out shopping for gear.

62
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:20,710
Oh, that's right.

63
00:05:20,793 --> 00:05:22,780
I should update my equipment, too.

64
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:25,632
I don't think this is going to be enough.

65
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,030
Okay.

66
00:05:27,113 --> 00:05:29,020
I know a good weapon shop in town.

67
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:30,497
But do you have enough money?

68
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:32,109
Because they're not cheap.

69
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:34,377
Okay, money.

70
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:36,977
Wait, this thing called
Yule, is that money?

71
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:37,890
Uh-huh.

72
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:43,160
Hey, Yui, wake up. We're heading out now.

73
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:45,410
Okay.

74
00:06:09,620 --> 00:06:10,738
Why'd we come here?

75
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:15,677
Well, when flying long distances, it's
better if you start from a higher altitude.

76
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:17,760
That's what the tower is here for.

77
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:19,580
Oh, that makes sense.

78
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,060
You're kidding me!

79
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:27,120
Come on, let's go!

80
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:29,693
I wanna get past the forest before dark.

81
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:37,020
This way, Slowpoke!

82
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:42,770
Leafa!

83
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:47,120
Oh, uh, hello, Sigurd.

84
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:49,597
What's this I hear about
you leaving the party?

85
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:50,510
Is that true?

86
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:52,600
Well, yeah, it is.

87
00:06:52,940 --> 00:06:56,897
Do you have any idea how much that's
going to upset the other members?

88
00:06:56,980 --> 00:07:00,397
You said it wouldn't be a problem if
I joined only when I had the time.

89
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:03,137
You also said I could
quit whenever I wanted to.

90
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:06,377
Yes, I know what I said, but you've
been with us for a while now.

91
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:07,577
Everyone knows you.

92
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:11,542
If you leave us, it's going to
damage the reputation of the party.

93
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:19,200
Party members are not items.

94
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:22,760
What did you say?

95
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:30,397
Party members aren't items, so don't
expect them to be on call for you.

96
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:31,657
They're not your armor.

97
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:32,777
They're not your sword.

98
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:34,377
They're not your equipment.

99
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:35,480
You son of a...

100
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:39,877
I bet that big mouth of yours got
you thrown out of your own territory.

101
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:42,917
Let's see what you got, you
piece of sprigging trash.

102
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,480
Okay, that's it. Enough.

103
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:47,708
Kirito's my new partner,
so leave him alone.

104
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,560
What? Leafa?

105
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:52,900
You're abandoning us to
be a renegade like him?

106
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:56,280
Yes, I am.

107
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:58,186
And I'm not coming back ever!

108
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:02,997
I don't give a damn about you
buzzing around my party members.

109
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:06,157
But if you think you can steal
them, then that's another story.

110
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:09,517
If you're stupid enough to waltz
into another race's territory,

111
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:13,012
then it's your own damn fault
if you get killed, Spriggan!

112
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,856
This isn't the time or place, Sigurd.

113
00:08:22,060 --> 00:08:26,413
If we gank this guy in front of all
these people, we're going to look bad.

114
00:08:35,540 --> 00:08:38,952
Once you cross our border, you
better run and hide, Leafa.

115
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:42,357
I never expected you to
betray me like this. Never.

116
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:44,597
But you'll regret it soon enough.

117
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:51,680
I'm

118
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:53,670
really

119
00:08:53,753 --> 00:08:54,583
sorry you got

120
00:08:54,666 --> 00:08:55,496
dragged into all that drama.

121
00:08:55,579 --> 00:08:56,409
It's cool.

122
00:08:56,492 --> 00:08:58,417
I'm worried about you though.

123
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:00,337
Are you sure about this?

124
00:09:00,420 --> 00:09:04,397
Hey!

125
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,540
Hey, don't!

126
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:12,550
Wow.

127
00:09:12,633 --> 00:09:14,100
This is an amazing view.

128
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:18,111
The sky's so close, it's like
I can reach out and touch it.

129
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:19,557
I know, right?

130
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:23,560
Whenever I look up at that sky,
everything else feels so small.

131
00:09:28,140 --> 00:09:30,552
The timing couldn't have been any better.

132
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:33,077
I've been thinking about
leaving here for a while now.

133
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:37,984
Okay, but I feel like it's sort of my fault
you left on bad terms with those guys.

134
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:42,486
Yeah, well, I don't think it
could have happened any other way.

135
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,460
What do you mean by renegade?

136
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:49,120
A renegade's a player who
abandons their territory.

137
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:52,900
If you get branded as one,
everyone's gonna look down on you.

138
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:54,829
And you're cool with that?

139
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:56,929
Yeah, I don't really care.

140
00:09:57,520 --> 00:10:02,057
But I don't understand why everyone's so
quick to tie each other down like that.

141
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:05,140
I mean, what's the point
in having wings, you know?

142
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,640
You humans are so complicated.

143
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:13,617
Honestly, your psychology is confusing.

144
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:17,197
Why do you act so horribly to each other
when all you want is companionship?

145
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:18,280
What do you mean?

146
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:21,960
If it were me, I'd do that.

147
00:10:22,380 --> 00:10:24,968
It's simple, straightforward,
and efficient.

148
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:27,060
That's an amazing AI.

149
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:30,601
Do all private pixies act
like that or just yours?

150
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:32,760
No, just mine, but she's a weirdo.

151
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:36,160
I guess you would know, huh?

152
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:39,040
All we want is companionship.

153
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:42,150
Lipia!

154
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:43,960
Hey, Recon.

155
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:45,500
How could you do this?

156
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:49,817
You could have at least said
something before you left.

157
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:50,730
Oh, sorry.

158
00:10:50,813 --> 00:10:51,643
I guess I forgot.

159
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:56,120
Why'd you quit the party
all of a sudden like that?

160
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:58,497
Well, I didn't really
think too hard about it.

161
00:10:58,580 --> 00:10:59,410
I just did it.

162
00:10:59,493 --> 00:11:01,221
What are you going to do, though?

163
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,520
As if, Leafa!

164
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:04,337
It doesn't matter where you go.

165
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:06,357
My sword belongs to you and you alone.

166
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:08,280
I don't need it, but thanks.

167
00:11:10,220 --> 00:11:13,157
What I meant by that was,
I'm going to go with you.

168
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:14,070
Wherever.

169
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:18,577
That is, I'd like to go, but there's
something that's been bugging me.

170
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:19,490
What is it?

171
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:21,800
I can't really prove anything yet.

172
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:24,597
But there's a few things I
want to look into some more,

173
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:27,657
so I'm going to stay in
Sigurd's party a little longer.

174
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:28,620
Hey, Kirito?

175
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:31,517
She has a habit of getting
herself in trouble.

176
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,977
I'd appreciate it if
you'd keep an eye on her.

177
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:34,890
Yeah, sure.

178
00:11:35,180 --> 00:11:36,240
Whatever you say.

179
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:39,157
And just to make sure
we're absolutely clear,

180
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,420
Lipa is my...

181
00:11:42,460 --> 00:11:44,872
We'll be in the neutral zone for a while.

182
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,522
Message me if you need anything.

183
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:49,840
Ow, ow, ow!

184
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:59,197
Let me get this straight.

185
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:02,217
In real life he's your friend,
yeah, something like that.

186
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:05,157
Hmm, okay, what's that weird noise?

187
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:08,777
Supposed to mean nothing,
just a little jealous is all.

188
00:12:08,860 --> 00:12:12,600
Now that person's
feelings I can understand.

189
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:15,057
He must like you a lot wouldn't you say?

190
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:17,657
LIPA, do you feel the same way about him?

191
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:21,280
I don't know, jeez.

192
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:34,957
Hurry up, you guys!

193
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:38,057
Let's try to make it all the way
to the lake without stopping.

194
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:39,020
Okay.

195
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:03,350
Unbelievable!

196
00:13:03,433 --> 00:13:04,737
You can be so stubborn.

197
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:08,337
Seriously, no matter what
I do, I can't hurt you.

198
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:10,297
It's not like that. Body's real.

199
00:13:10,380 --> 00:13:13,277
Why can't you just loosen up
and enjoy yourself a little?

200
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:15,997
I don't expect you to understand,

201
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:19,617
but to me it doesn't matter
if my body's real or virtual.

202
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:22,037
You may not think that way, but I do.

203
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:24,937
Are you afraid you're going
to be corrupted somehow?

204
00:13:25,020 --> 00:13:27,197
Because if that's the case, you...

205
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:30,397
You definitely need to take things a
little less seriously while you're here.

206
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:32,997
Well, I'm not planning on
staying in this cage forever.

207
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:33,910
You'll see.

208
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:37,420
He'll come and save me. Really? Who will?

209
00:13:37,940 --> 00:13:39,880
That hero boyfriend of yours?

210
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:42,060
Goes by the name of Kirito?

211
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:45,790
Please.

212
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,377
You think I didn't know?

213
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:49,200
His real name's Kirigaya.

214
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:51,200
I met him the other day.

215
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:52,540
In the real world.

216
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:58,097
I couldn't believe that
weak little boy was

217
00:13:58,180 --> 00:14:00,137
the same one who beat *sword art online*.

218
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:04,697
It took me a second to collect myself,
by the way—where do you think I met him?

219
00:14:04,780 --> 00:14:05,610
In

220
00:14:05,740 --> 00:14:08,617
your hospital room as
you were lying there,

221
00:14:08,700 --> 00:14:10,677
I told him I'd be marrying you next week.

222
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:15,497
My god, you should have seen his face—it
was like all the color drained out of it.

223
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:17,517
I could barely keep myself from laughing.

224
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:21,237
Do you want to know what I think?

225
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,817
I'll bet you anything that brat won't have

226
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:26,017
the guts to put on the
nerve gear ever again.

227
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:32,017
That reminds me—I promised him I was
going to send along a wedding invitation.

228
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:36,437
I'm pretty sure he'll come; he's going
to want to see you in your wedding dress.

229
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:37,797
I know I'm generous.

230
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:41,137
The least I can do is leave
the little hero a few crumbs.

231
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:42,420
a few crumbs

232
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:51,520
Well, I have to get going now, Titania.

233
00:14:52,020 --> 00:14:54,020
I hope you don't miss me too much.

234
00:14:57,660 --> 00:14:58,780
He's alive.

235
00:15:00,940 --> 00:15:02,020
Kirito's alive.

236
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:36,320
Eight, one, one, three,
two, three, two, nine.

237
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:58,960
Nice job.

238
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:01,185
Thanks for the awesome backup.

239
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:06,657
Our wings aren't going
to last much longer.

240
00:16:06,740 --> 00:16:08,697
I think we should land
down there for a bit.

241
00:16:08,780 --> 00:16:09,610
Okay.

242
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,788
Hey, you getting tired yet?

243
00:16:20,500 --> 00:16:21,330
Nope.

244
00:16:21,413 --> 00:16:22,243
I'm good to go.

245
00:16:22,326 --> 00:16:23,200
Okay, Mr. Tough Guy.

246
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:27,397
I hate to break it to you, but flying's
out for both of us for a little while.

247
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:28,900
Huh? How come?

248
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:31,256
You see that mountain way over there?

249
00:16:31,420 --> 00:16:34,317
It's above the altitude
limit, so we can't fly over.

250
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:37,477
The only way anyone can pass
it is to go through the caves.

251
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:41,077
It's the toughest part of the trip
between Sylph Territory and Arun.

252
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:42,180
Or so I've heard.

253
00:16:42,540 --> 00:16:44,716
I've never even been this far myself.

254
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:45,980
Guess we walk.

255
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:49,300
These caves, are they long? Pretty long.

256
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:51,737
There's a mining town about halfway.

257
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:54,137
It's neutral territory,
so we can rest there.

258
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:55,220
That reminds me.

259
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:57,337
Are you good for time, or
do you have to get back?

260
00:16:57,420 --> 00:16:59,655
It's seven at night in the real world.

261
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:01,737
Yeah, I can keep going for a while.

262
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:02,650
Cool.

263
00:17:02,733 --> 00:17:04,244
I can too, so let's keep going.

264
00:17:04,380 --> 00:17:06,657
But since we're here,
we should rotate out.

265
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:08,280
Wait, rotate? Yeah.

266
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:12,057
We take turns logging out and
resting while the other keeps watch.

267
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:14,897
You can't log out when you're
in the field, remember?

268
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:16,977
So we have to take turns logging out.

269
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:19,837
The person who stays behind
guards the other's avatar.

270
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:21,500
Okay, sounds like a plan.

271
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:22,950
Ladies first.

272
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,631
Okay, don't mind if I do.

273
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:26,907
See you in about 20 minutes.

274
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:35,730
Ah!

275
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,765
Hey, Kazuto, what do you
want to do for dinner?

276
00:17:56,660 --> 00:17:58,300
I wonder if he's asleep.

277
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:22,840
I can't wait to get back there.

278
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:36,030
Kirito.

279
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:40,197
It's not that I'm in love
with him or anything,

280
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:43,221
or that I've got someone
to go on adventures with.

281
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:44,430
No.

282
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:47,880
I'm just excited I get to
go places in a new world.

283
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:01,420
Hey, I'm back!

284
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,151
Did you see any monsters?

285
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:04,460
No, I didn't.

286
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:06,737
It's been pretty quiet this whole time.

287
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:07,937
What are you eating?

288
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:10,961
I bought a bunch at a shop
before we left Sylvain.

289
00:19:11,740 --> 00:19:15,277
I don't know what they're called, but
an NPC said you can only get them there.

290
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:17,007
I've never seen them before.

291
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:31,337
Sorry to leave you like
this, but it is my turn.

292
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:32,580
Keep me safe, okay?

293
00:19:32,820 --> 00:19:34,820
Get out of here before I hurt you!

294
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:52,170
No way!

295
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:54,177
You can move when your
master's logged out?

296
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:55,860
Well, of course I can move.

297
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:57,760
You know, I'm my own person.

298
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:01,649
And for your information, he's
not my master, he's my daddy.

299
00:20:02,280 --> 00:20:03,340
Yeah, about that.

300
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:06,577
I was going to ask you before,
why do you call him your daddy?

301
00:20:06,660 --> 00:20:09,860
Did he, you know, set you
that way or something?

302
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:12,517
He didn't do anything to my settings.

303
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:13,480
He saved me.

304
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:15,525
He told me I was his daughter.

305
00:20:15,740 --> 00:20:17,152
That makes him my daddy.

306
00:20:17,560 --> 00:20:18,913
You see how that works?

307
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:20,520
Yeah, I guess.

308
00:20:22,580 --> 00:20:24,540
Do you, you know, like him?

309
00:20:26,100 --> 00:20:27,100
I'm sorry.

310
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:29,792
I don't understand what you mean by like.

311
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:31,957
Are you serious?

312
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:34,377
It means you want to be
with him all the time,

313
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:37,737
and when you're together you get
excited about being near him.

314
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,580
Or something like that.

315
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:46,500
What's wrong, Leafa? Nothing.
It's nothing. What's nothing?

316
00:20:46,740 --> 00:20:47,681
What's going on?

317
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:49,590
What is it?

318
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:51,315
Did something happen?

319
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:52,896
Welcome back, Daddy.

320
00:20:53,420 --> 00:20:56,797
Leafa was just explaining to me
what it means when someone said...

321
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:57,710
No!

322
00:20:57,793 --> 00:20:58,623
I said it's nothing.

323
00:20:58,706 --> 00:20:59,536
It's nothing.

324
00:20:59,619 --> 00:21:01,340
You weren't there for very long.

325
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:03,477
I hope you got something to eat.

326
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:04,390
Yeah.

327
00:21:04,473 --> 00:21:06,847
My family left something
for me, so I'm good.

328
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:07,930
Sweet.

329
00:21:08,013 --> 00:21:08,843
Come on, then.

330
00:21:08,926 --> 00:21:09,756
Let's get going.

331
00:21:11,500 --> 00:21:12,880
Oh, okay.

332
00:21:13,320 --> 00:21:14,920
All right, lead the way.

333
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:19,420
Is something wrong? I don't know.

334
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:22,407
It sort of felt like
someone was watching us.

335
00:21:23,060 --> 00:21:25,354
Hey, Yui, there are any players nearby?

336
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:27,955
No, I'm not sensing any other players.

337
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:31,140
It's possible someone put a tracer on us.

338
00:21:31,320 --> 00:21:32,677
What the heck's a tracer?

339
00:21:32,760 --> 00:21:34,231
A kind of tracking magic.

340
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,911
It looks like a small animal or an insect.

341
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:39,057
It tells the caster a target's position.

342
00:21:39,140 --> 00:21:40,117
Can you dispel it?

343
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:42,040
Sure, if you can find it.

344
00:21:42,320 --> 00:21:45,097
The thing is, if the
caster's magic skill is high,

345
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:47,057
the tracer can track you from far away.

346
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:50,140
In a field this size, it'd
take forever to find it.

347
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,030
Great.

348
00:21:52,113 --> 00:21:53,739
Eh, maybe it's just my imagination.

349
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:56,160
Come on, let's go. Okay.

350
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:11,847
I'm going to take your hand.

351
00:22:12,620 --> 00:22:13,557
I'm going to take your hand.

352
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:18,480
I will be praying. I will be praying.

353
00:22:24,380 --> 00:22:25,439
I will be praying.

354
00:22:33,460 --> 00:22:35,380
The end of the day of the night

355
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:05,300
Thank you so much for watching.

356
00:23:35,380 --> 00:23:38,800
Next time, the Legrou Corridor.
